r anyone within  the organization whether it's the  accounting team or the payroll team  while this was convenient it also  required that the company maintain a  database this might be viable for  someone like IBM or Xerox but the local  Factory had no idea how to operate or  maintain a database so in addition to  the system sap also offered regular  maintenance and upgrades and this is  where the money was really at first this  was actually super easy given that there  was plenty of downtime these systems  were only used during the day Monday  through Friday so you could upgrade the  system during nights and on the weekend  but nowadays there isn't nearly as big  of a window given that downtime is  extremely expensive in the modern world  so sap has had to become quite creative  when it comes to maintenance and the  upgrades anyway sap would further refine  the system and create their first  Flagship product the sap R1 Sap's first  customer was a chemical company in  Germany but it didn't take them long to  onboard a bunch of local companies and  from there and didn't take long for sap  to become the go-to company for  all-in-one back-end Solutions  over the years sap has grown their  product line aggressively in fact they  currently offered 309 products but most  of this can be watered down into five  main categories starting with sap Erp or  sap enterprise resource planning this is  really the core of sap and it covers all  of the main functions that any business  would need this includes Supply Chain  management product lifecycle management  human Capital Management financial  management and customer relationship  management all of these accomplish  exactly what they sound like the Supply  Chain management software for example  helps companies keep track of inventory  analyze demand create projections of  Supply requirements manage Logistics and  so on similarly the financial management  software makes it easy to track  expenditures calculate taxes manage your  